CLAUDE.md:1312  > **THE FLOOR.** A detector is VACUOUS �?" replace it IN-ROUND �?" unless it (a) fails on the
CLAUDE.md:1313  > pre-fix build, (b) fails on a **VERBATIM REINSTATEMENT of the removed defect at EVERY fixed
CLAUDE.md:1314  > site**, and (c) fails on a **NULL MEDIUM** -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under
CLAUDE.md:1315  > test (the clause-(c) block below says what that is per instrument kind). Below the floor, the
CLAUDE.md:1316  > round's own claim to have "shipped a detector with the fix" is a WRONG RECORD, which the
CLAUDE.md:1317  > stopping rule already fixes in-round.
CLAUDE.md:1318  >
CLAUDE.md:1319  > ### *** CLAUSE (c) -- WHAT A NULL MEDIUM IS, AND THE TWO WAYS TO RECORD IT.  Ruled 2026-10-09 by the
CLAUDE.md:1320  > ### flagship seat (Fable 5.1, queue 7n-1 / 7n-2), confirmed by GPT-6 Astra with corrections, written
CLAUDE.md:1321  > ### here by owner ruling.  The gloss it replaces -- "a stale copy, a comment-only file -- i.e. it
CLAUDE.md:1322  > ### carries identity rows" -- is deleted, not demoted. ***
CLAUDE.md:1323  >
CLAUDE.md:1324  > **ONE criterion -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under test -- and its object
CLAUDE.md:1325  > differs by instrument kind:**
CLAUDE.md:1326  > * an offline differential that `#include`s the product: a COMMENT-ONLY product source, which must
CLAUDE.md:1327  >   fail to COMPILE, with a gate that reds on the compile failure (measured for `#488`:
CLAUDE.md:1328  >   `regress/artifacts/shortread/nullmedium_20261009/RECEIPT.txt`);
CLAUDE.md:1329  > * a runtime probe: an ABSENT or NON-EMULATOR binary (every session dies), or a build WITHOUT the
CLAUDE.md:1330  >   device for a device round;
CLAUDE.md:1331  > * an instruction-handler round: an IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- the
CLAUDE.md:1332  >   recommended default, two measured legs at `#527`.
CLAUDE.md:1333  >
