*** AND A LISTED `.txt` CAN BE EMPTY.  `idt_r30xx.txt` WAS A ZERO-BYTE FILE FROM 2026-07-25 UNTIL 2026-10-01 WHILE THE
LIST ABOVE NAMED IT AS THE THING TO GREP.  Found 2026-10-01, re-extracted the same day with git-bash
`/mingw64/bin/pdftotext -layout`: 1,071,238 bytes, 22,370 lines (`wc -c`, `wc -l`); the empty original is kept beside it
as `idt_r30xx.txt.EMPTY_20260725`. ***

A grep of a zero-byte file reports NOTHING FOR EVERYTHING -- the pattern-that-selected-nothing class, with the manual
itself as the empty set -- so for ten weeks any "the R30xx manual does not say" would have been a phantom absence.
**`wc -c _scratchpad/<manual>.txt` before trusting an absence in it; a listing proves the file exists, not that it
has text.**

