 succeeded in 352ms:
+#  THE CONFIGURED COMPILER IS A COMMAND, NOT A NAME.  configure writes CC= into the generated
+#  Makefiles, and a tree configured with CC="gcc -m32" builds the product with both words, which no
+#  pinned banner can tell from plain gcc.  So the WHOLE string is passed (the driver shell-splits it
+#  and uses all of it for every compiler operation, the identity line and the census included) and
+#  the check here is only that its first word resolves.
+SRTREECC=$(sed -n 's/^CC=//p' "$SRMK")
+check "sysasic: the configured tree's CC command resolves" \
+      "$([ -n "$SRTREECC" ] && command -v "${SRTREECC%% *}" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo yes || echo "no: CC=[$SRTREECC]")" "yes"
+#  THE POPULATION the census reads, counted LEXICALLY: FILES under src/ that spell the include at
+#  the start of a line, in quotes or angle brackets, in a .c or a .h (a header in src/ that spells
+#  it is counted as that header).  Anchored, because an unanchored LINE count is 5 at e483d931:
+#  dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c quotes the include in a comment (`git grep -n
+#  'thirdparty/dreamcast_sysasicvar' -- src').  Pinned by EQUALITY at the four TUs the census
+#  names, so a fifth file that spells it reds here.  WHAT IT IS NOT: a census of the translation
+#  units that reach the header -- a wrapper header can take an includer out of this count while a
+#  fifth TU reaches the header through it, and a macro-generated or out-of-tree include is not
+#  counted at all.
+check "sysasic census: files under src/ that #include the header (a lexical count)" \
