## Q1

No macro edit inside that denominator passes both legs and sits outside the EQUIVALENT and DISCLOSED media.

Walked, not inferred:

- Integer sweep is `range(-1024, 8192)` = 9216 values, of which 0..95 are the 96 in-domain lines. Samples are 54, of which 22 have Python values in 0..95 (`'A'`, `0x5f`, `(char)95`, and 0/95 in long long, unsigned long long, long, unsigned long, unsigned int, short, unsigned short, char, signed char, unsigned char). Out-of-domain lines: 9120 + 32 = 9152. 9216 + 54 = 9270. One-token bound moves (`< 95`, `< 97`, `>= 1`, `> -1`) hit A0, A95, X96, Xm1, or a swept line on both routes.
- Address `0x5f6900 + 4*(e>>5)` against the twelve `switch` labels in `dev_dreamcast_asic.c` (0/4/8, 0x10/14/18, 0x20/24/28, 0x30/34/38). In-domain ints land only on pending_irq words +0x00/+0x04/+0x08. TVAL checks that address for every int in 0..95; SWEEP's typedefs check it on ADDR, including the eight classes at 0 and 95.
- Clobber, same formula, no extra mask on `e`: [128,223], [256,351], [384,479] are 96+96+96 = 288 events on the nine mask words. [224,255] and [352,383] are 32+32 = 64 dropped. Span [128,479] is 479�^'128+1 = 352. Those values are refusals, so a different out-of-domain address is not a compiled product.
- Payload: device tests bit 32, then stores `uint32_t`. TVAL pins low 32 and bit 32 for all 96 ints. ID pins all 64 bits at the 21 defines (2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 19, 21, 32, 33, 34, 35, 66, 67). None of those 21 has `(e & 31) == 31`.
